---
source: crates/agent-compose/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&output)
---
Compile a spec to a TypeScript project (validates first; emits only when clean; `--restamp` instead rewrites a built tree's hash to what its files hash to)

Usage: agent-compose build [OPTIONS] <PATH>

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          Path to the spec entrypoint (conventionally `main.yml`)

Options:
      --target <NAME>
          Deploy target to resolve and emit for
          
          [default: local]

      --out <DIR>
          Where to write the generated project [default: <project>/build/<target>]

      --check
          Write nothing; report whether the directory already matches the spec

      --restamp
          Recompute `ARTIFACT_HASH` over the output directory as it stands, after a hand edit; reads no spec and builds nothing

      --format <FORMAT>
          How to report what was found

          Possible values:
          - human: Written for a person, on stderr
          - json:  One JSON object on stdout
          
          [default: human]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
